---
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = '20 September 2026';
const connectionUrl = 'https://connect.canopy.ag/mcp';
---

<Layout
  title="Canopy connector | Canopy"
  description="Connect Canopy to an AI assistant and ask about your operation in plain language."
>
  <div class="legal">
    <div class="shell legal__inner">
      <p class="section-kicker">Connector</p>
      <h1>Connecting Canopy to an AI assistant</h1>
      <p class="legal__lead">
        The Canopy connector lets an AI assistant read your Canopy data so you can ask
        about your operation in plain language, without leaving the conversation:
        what a zone did overnight, which schedules ran, what a crew logged.
      </p>
      <p class="legal__meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        The connector is in <strong>limited access</strong> while we verify it with a
        small number of growers. It is not yet open to every Canopy account. If you
        would like to be part of that group, email
        <a href="mailto:hello@canopy.ag">hello@canopy.ag</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The connection address</h2>
      <p>
        Assistants that support connectors ask for a URL. Canopy's is:
      </p>
      <p><code>{connectionUrl}</code></p>
      <p>
        This address is only for the connector. It is not the address you use to sign in
        to Canopy in a browser, and it is separate from the tools our own team uses.
      </p>

      <h2>Signing in</h2>
      <p>
        You sign in with the same Canopy account you already use. The assistant sends you
        to a Canopy page, you sign in there, and you are shown exactly what the assistant
        is asking to do before you agree to anything. You can decline, and nothing is
        shared.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your password is never given to the assistant. Canopy signs you in, and the
        assistant only ever receives permission to act as you, which you can withdraw.
      </p>

      <h2>What it can reach</h2>
      <p>
        Only your own organization's data. The connector cannot see another Canopy
        customer's operation, and it cannot see the internal tools our team uses to run
        the platform.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>It cannot operate your equipment.</strong> The connector cannot start or
        stop irrigation, open or close a valve, or switch a relay. Those actions stay in
        the Canopy app and with our team. An assistant connected to Canopy can tell you
        what happened; it cannot make water move.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions, and turning it off</h2>
      <p>
        Disconnecting is done in the assistant, and takes effect immediately. For anything
        else, including a request to remove data, write to
        <a href="mailto:hello@canopy.ag">hello@canopy.ag</a>; see
        <a href="/support">support</a> for what to include.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/terms">terms</a> apply to
        the connector exactly as they do to the rest of Canopy.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
